s won’t be able to view the eclipse but having a few webcams really helps to get the feeling!Hoping to be able to see the great eclipse of 2027 live ;-)https://www.timeanddate.com/eclipse/solar/2027-august-2replydorienh 10 minutes ago | prev | next [–] Sad to be in Singapore where eclipse is not visible!replyxanthine 1 hour ago | prev | next [–] Sorry for my ignorance, but can someone please explain what I'm looking at here?replymsdz 1 hour ago | parent | next [–] About five hours from now, the sections of Europe indicated on the map will experience a total solar eclipse, with other regions of the continent experiencing a partial one.The map shows feeds to watch it.replyembedding-shape 1 hour ago | parent | prev | next [–] Today there is a eclipse, the map shows where the eclipse will be. In the path of the eclipse, there are also a ton of live webcams, and this map shows those and let you preview the webcams. Does it make sense now?replyrob74 48 minutes ago | root | parent | next [–] Even more specifically, it will start off over Greenland, continue over western Iceland and then finish with the sunset in northeastern Spain and the Balearic Islands.replyvoidUpdate 40 minutes ago | root | parent | next [–] If you pan to the right, it shows that it actually starts in a bit of russiareplymatsemann 50 minutes ago | prev | next [–] https://www.timeanddate.com/eclipse/solar/2026-august-12Nice page showing where it will be, with times and visualizations for any point/city.replyhno8a34nwn 17 minutes ago | prev | next [–] Was just dealing with this yesterdayreply4gotunameagain 58 minutes ago | prev | next [–] Really cool. I'm quite curious as to where the webcam data came from, as it seems to be from various websites/sources.replyv-mdev 0 minutes ago | parent | next [–] I'm curious tooreplychristkv 15 minutes ago | prev | next [–] We are going to get the full solar eclipse, but to be honest I'm going to enjoy the transitions more than the actual eclipse itself. It's not like